---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaptureBlock from '../components/CaptureBlock.astro';
import SafetyAlert from '../components/SafetyAlert.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Stay Safe: Practical Safety Tools"
  description="Evidence-informed safety tools, monitored-device guidance, emergency resources, coercive-control and stalking guides, and practical options without fear or blame."
>
  <SafetyAlert />

  <article class="safety-hub wrap">
    <header class="safety-hero">
      <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Stay Safe</p>
      <h1>Stay Safe</h1>
      <p class="safety-hero__promise">Practical, evidence-informed tools to help you understand risk, preserve your options, and stay safer&mdash;without fear, spectacle, or victim blame.</p>
      <p class="safety-boundary">Safety information may help people recognize patterns, document conduct, consider options, and reach appropriate support. It cannot predict or prevent every act of harm. Responsibility always belongs to the person causing harm&mdash;not the person targeted.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="safety-paths" aria-label="Choose a safety pathway">
      <a class="safety-path safety-path--urgent" href="#immediate-help"><span class="safety-path__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><strong>Immediate Help</strong><span>Emergency and crisis contacts first. No email required.</span></a>
      <a class="safety-path" href="#recognize-pattern"><span class="safety-path__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><strong>Recognize a Pattern</strong><span>Coercive control and stalking guidance without diagnosis or prediction.</span></a>
      <a class="safety-path" href="#practical-tools"><span class="safety-path__number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><strong>Practical Safety Tools</strong><span>Digital safety, documentation, planning, and support options.</span></a>
    </nav>

    <section class="safety-section immediate" id="immediate-help" aria-labelledby="immediate-help-title">
      <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Ungated resources</p>
      <h2 id="immediate-help-title">Immediate Help</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">These contacts are U.S.-based. Outside the United States, use your local emergency number and qualified local survivor services.</p>
      <div class="help-grid">
        <article class="help-card help-card--emergency">
          <h3>Immediate physical danger or urgent medical help</h3>
          <p>Call <a class="help-number" href="tel:911">911</a> or your local emergency services when it is safe to do so.</p>
          <p class="help-note">911 is for immediate danger and emergency response.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-card">
          <h3>Suicide, mental-health, or substance-use crisis</h3>
          <p>Call or text <a class="help-number" href="tel:988">988</a>, or use <a href="https://988lifeline.org/get-help/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">988 Lifeline chat</a>.</p>
          <p class="help-note">988 provides crisis support. It does not replace 911 for immediate physical danger.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-card">
          <h3>Domestic violence or coercive control</h3>
          <p><a href="https://www.thehotline.org/get-help/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Domestic Violence Hotline</a>: call <a href="tel:18007997233">800-799-SAFE (7233)</a> or text <a href="sms:88788?body=START">START to 88788</a>.</p>
          <p class="help-note">Free, confidential advocate support is available 24/7.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-card">
          <h3>Sexual assault support</h3>
          <p><a href="https://rainn.org/help-and-healing/hotline/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RAINN National Sexual Assault Hotline</a>: call <a href="tel:18006564673">800-656-HOPE (4673)</a> or text <a href="sms:64673?body=HOPE">HOPE to 64673</a>.</p>
          <p class="help-note">Free, confidential support is available 24/7.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-card">
          <h3>Human trafficking support</h3>
          <p><a href="https://humantraffickinghotline.org/en/get-help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Human Trafficking Hotline</a>: call <a href="tel:18883737888">888-373-7888</a> or text <a href="sms:233733">233733</a>.</p>
          <p class="help-note">Specialized support and referrals are available 24/7.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="resource-boundary"><strong>NEP is not an emergency, counseling, medical, or legal service.</strong> You never need to subscribe, buy anything, or read a case file to use the resources above.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section" id="recognize-pattern" aria-labelledby="recognize-pattern-title">
      <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Understand, do not diagnose</p>
      <h2 id="recognize-pattern-title">Recognize a Pattern</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">A concerning behavior may deserve attention without proving what will happen next. Look for repetition, persistence, loss of freedom, boundary violations, or escalation. A trained advocate can help consider the full context without pushing you toward a predetermined choice.</p>
      <div class="guide-grid">
        <a class="guide-card" href="/post/what-is-coercive-control-the-signs-examples-and-what-to-do/">
          <span class="guide-card__label">Focused guide</span>
          <h3>Coercive Control: Recognizing Patterns and Considering Options</h3>
          <p>Understand patterns of power and control, possible signs, technology concerns, and options for support&mdash;without treating a checklist as a diagnosis.</p>
          <span class="guide-card__go">Read the guide &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="guide-card" href="/post/stalking-documentation-digital-safety-finding-help/">
          <span class="guide-card__label">Focused guide</span>
          <h3>Stalking: Documentation, Digital Safety, and Finding Help</h3>
          <p>Learn how patterns may appear across channels, what may be useful to preserve, and why safety planning should come before abrupt technology changes.</p>
          <span class="guide-card__go">Read the guide &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="calibration"><strong>Risk factors are not predictions.</strong> A documented factor can help a specialist assess context; it cannot guarantee that harm will or will not occur, and no public checklist can evaluate an individual situation.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section" id="practical-tools" aria-labelledby="practical-tools-title">
      <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Preserve your options</p>
      <h2 id="practical-tools-title">Practical Safety Tools</h2>
      <div class="tool-list">
        <article><h3>Use a safer device when monitoring is possible</h3><p>If someone may have access to your phone, accounts, vehicle, or connected devices, consider using a different device before researching help. Abruptly removing access or a tracker can sometimes alert the person monitoring you. Review the <a href="https://www.techsafety.org/resources-survivors/technology-safety-plan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safety Net Project technology plan</a>.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Document only when it is safe for you</h3><p>A dated record may help show a pattern if you later seek advocacy, workplace, school, civil, or criminal-justice support. Storage location and device access matter. SPARC provides a <a href="https://www.stalkingawareness.org/documentation-log/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">stalking documentation log and handbook</a>.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Build a plan around your real responsibilities</h3><p>A personalized plan may consider communication, transportation, medications, documents, money, children, pets, work, school, disability access, and the risks of different choices. A trained advocate can help without ordering you to leave. Start with the Hotline&rsquo;s <a href="https://www.thehotline.org/plan-for-safety/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">safety-planning resources</a>.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Keep first meetings flexible and public when practical</h3><p>For a first meeting with someone known online, options may include verifying identity through another channel, choosing a public staffed location, arranging your own transportation, and telling a trusted person your plan. These are options, not guarantees; the person causing harm remains responsible. See RAINN&rsquo;s <a href="https://rainn.org/strategies-to-reduce-risk-increase-safety/tips-for-safer-dating-online-and-in-person/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">safer-dating guidance</a>.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Help without taking away autonomy</h3><p>Listen without judgment, ask what would be useful, and avoid ultimatums that may increase isolation. The person closest to the situation often knows risks that are not visible to others. The Hotline offers guidance for <a href="https://www.thehotline.org/resources/safety-planning-for-friends-and-family/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">friends and family</a>.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section safety-email" id="safety-updates" aria-labelledby="safety-updates-title">
      <h2 id="safety-updates-title" class="sr-only">Optional safety and court updates</h2>
      <CaptureBlock offer="safety" content="safety_hub" />
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section court-bridge" aria-labelledby="court-bridge-title">
      <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Safety and the public record</p>
      <h2 id="court-bridge-title">What the record can teach us&mdash;without blaming the victim.</h2>
      <p>When a court record supports a practical lesson, NEP may explain the documented behavior and the limits of the evidence. One case does not predict another. No safety choice transfers responsibility away from the person who caused harm.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/court-calendar/">Open the verified Court Calendar &rarr;</a></p>
      <p class="help-note">The optional subscriber form above connects practical safety tools with <em>This Week in Court</em>. Emergency and crisis resources remain separate and ungated.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
      <h2 id="sources-title">Sources and review standard</h2>
      <p>Reviewed August 9, 2026. Material safety and contact information on this hub was checked against the <a href="https://www.thehotline.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Domestic Violence Hotline</a>, <a href="https://www.stalkingawareness.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SPARC</a>, <a href="https://www.techsafety.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NNEDV Safety Net Project</a>, <a href="https://988lifeline.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">988 Lifeline</a>, <a href="https://rainn.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RAINN</a>, <a href="https://humantraffickinghotline.org/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Human Trafficking Hotline</a>, and <a href="https://www.womenslaw.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WomensLaw</a>.</p>
      <p>This is general education, not individualized legal, medical, emergency, or safety advice. Services, laws, and risks vary by location and circumstance.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .safety-hub{max-width:1040px;padding-top:54px}
  .safety-hero{max-width:790px}
  .safety-hero h1{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(42px,7vw,72px);line-height:1;margin:10px 0 16px}
  .safety-hero__promise{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(23px,3.4vw,34px);line-height:1.28;margin:0 0 18px;color:var(--ink)}
  .safety-boundary,.calibration,.resource-boundary{padding:18px 20px;border-left:3px solid var(--accent);background:var(--bg-2);border-radius:0 9px 9px 0;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6}
  .safety-paths{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin:36px 0 56px}
  .safety-path{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;min-height:190px;padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:12px;background:var(--bg-2);transition:border-color .16s,transform .16s}
  .safety-path:hover{border-color:var(--accent);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .safety-path:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}
  .safety-path strong{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:25px;line-height:1.15}
  .safety-path span:last-child{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:15px;line-height:1.5}
  .safety-path__number{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.12em}
  .safety-path--urgent{border-color:rgba(217,166,92,.55)}
  .safety-section{scroll-margin-top:92px;margin:0 0 66px}
  .safety-section h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(31px,4.5vw,44px);line-height:1.1;margin:8px 0 14px}
  .section-lede{font-size:18px;color:var(--ink-2);max-width:72ch;margin:0 0 24px}
  .help-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:14px}
  .help-card{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:11px;background:var(--bg-2)}
  .help-card--emergency{border:2px solid #d9a65c}
  .help-card h3,.tool-list h3{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 10px}
  .help-card p{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--ink-2)}
  .help-card a,.tool-list a,.sources a{color:#ff8064;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .help-number{font-size:1.25em;font-weight:800}
  .help-note{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-3)!important}
  .resource-boundary{margin-top:18px}
  .guide-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}
  .guide-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:290px;padding:26px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(155deg,var(--bg-2),#15110f)}
  .guide-card:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
  .guide-card:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}
  .guide-card__label{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}
  .guide-card h3{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:28px;line-height:1.12;margin:12px 0}
  .guide-card p{color:var(--ink-2);margin:0 0 20px}
  .guide-card__go{margin-top:auto;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
  .calibration{margin-top:18px}
  .tool-list{display:grid;gap:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .tool-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(210px,.7fr) 1.3fr;gap:28px;padding:24px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .tool-list p{margin:0;color:var(--ink-2)}
  .safety-email{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px}
  .court-bridge,.sources{padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--bg-2)}
  .sources p{color:var(--ink-2)}
  .sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}
  @media(max-width:760px){.safety-hub{padding:38px 18px 0}.safety-paths,.help-grid,.guide-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.safety-path{min-height:0}.tool-list article{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}.court-bridge,.sources{padding:22px}.safety-section{margin-bottom:48px}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.safety-path:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
